section: compiler
synopsis: Fix the RISC-V NCG failing to truncate the result of immediate subword add/sub/or operations
issues: #28133
mrs: !17000

description: {
  The immediate fast paths for ``MO_Add``, ``MO_Sub`` and ``MO_Or`` emitted the
  operation without truncating the result to the operation width. For subword
  widths this violated the zero-extended subword invariant whenever the first
  operand was a subword local, so a later zero-extending widening conversion
  (a plain ``MOV`` on RV64) exposed the stray high bits.

  The results are now truncated, as the immediate shift fast paths already did.
  ``MO_And`` needs no change: its operands are zero-extended and ``andi`` always
  leaves a result that is already in range.
}
